WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.126 --> 00:00:03.269
- [Voiceover] In the
forests of Southeast Asia,

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:07.410
high up in the treetops, a
mythical creature lives.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:09.025
It turns out dragons are real.

00:00:09.025 --> 00:00:11.525
It turns out dragons are real.

00:00:14.483 --> 00:00:16.794
So I have to call a biologist.

00:00:16.794 --> 00:00:18.187
- [Voiceover] I'm Anthony Russell,

00:00:18.187 --> 00:00:20.083
from the Department of Biological Sciences

00:00:20.083 --> 00:00:23.187
at the University of
Calgary in Alberta, Canada.

00:00:23.187 --> 00:00:24.020
- [Voiceover] We're talking

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.969
about a species of flying lizards.

00:00:25.969 --> 00:00:28.198
- [Voiceover] So it's called Draco Volans,

00:00:28.198 --> 00:00:30.267
which means flying dragon.

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:31.871
- [Voiceover] Okay, these flying dragons,

00:00:31.871 --> 00:00:33.005
they are a little different

00:00:33.005 --> 00:00:35.698
from the dragons we see in movies.

00:00:35.698 --> 00:00:37.674
For starters, they're small.

00:00:37.674 --> 00:00:39.026
- [Voiceover] They are, they are.

00:00:39.026 --> 00:00:41.259
- [Voiceover] Only about eight inches long

00:00:41.259 --> 00:00:43.173
and they don't breath fire.

00:00:43.173 --> 00:00:44.006
But, they do fly.

00:00:45.738 --> 00:00:46.571
In a way.

00:00:47.482 --> 00:00:49.490
They're gliders, which means they

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:52.419
have control of their
descent and trajectory,

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:54.337
but they don't have any power in it.

00:00:54.337 --> 00:00:57.053
- [Voiceover] For every
one foot they go down in

00:00:57.053 --> 00:01:01.254
vertical distance, they'll be
able to travel six feet along.

00:01:01.254 --> 00:01:02.129
- [Voiceover] And that's because

00:01:02.129 --> 00:01:03.837
they don't actually have wings.

00:01:03.837 --> 00:01:06.163
- [Voiceover] They're actually
modifications of the ribs,

00:01:06.163 --> 00:01:08.730
so they're nothing to do
with the legs and arms.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:10.627
- [Voiceover] Evolutionarily speaking,

00:01:10.627 --> 00:01:12.463
this has helped the lizards survive.

00:01:12.463 --> 00:01:16.905
They can escape attacks and
they have a broader living zone.

00:01:16.905 --> 00:01:19.497
So they might not be dragon dragons.

00:01:19.497 --> 00:01:20.889
- [Voiceover] Though
sometimes people name things

00:01:20.889 --> 00:01:23.623
because it's more dramatic effect.

00:01:23.623 --> 00:01:25.840
- [Voiceover] Well they're
still incredible lizards.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:27.488
Actually, no, you know what?

00:01:27.488 --> 00:01:30.238
I'm still gonna call 'em dragons.

